  "historicalEvidence": "validation.json and its original evidence, pre-GPL summaries, and first-release client baseline retain their actual original hashes and outcomes. They are not counted as new final-GPL runtime tests.",
  "remoteCI": "Published separately in release notes after the source commit is pushed; local binary hashes are not asserted to equal independent CI archive hashes.",
  "limitations": [
    "Self-reported device hashes, mod inventories and VM indicators are forgeable; no hardware attestation or all-cheat/all-VM coverage claim.",
    "Four rendered client cases test load, login, report, survival restoration and clean exit, not full gameplay, pack compatibility, authenticated production UUIDs or cheat efficacy.",
    "Login-stage timeout attempts are preserved separately in the final client report; passing retries do not erase these failures or establish their cause.",
    "Modern Bukkit branch fixtures shorten the report deadline and raise synthetic-account quotas; only the rendered-client and legacy default-policy suites exercise their separately recorded default configuration.",
    "Five old Paper tests used the pre-GPL candidate plus exact class-byte equivalence; old matching companion adapters, 1.18.2/1.19.4 development runtime work, Folia, proxies, hybrids, Geyser and sustained performance require separate acceptance.",
    "Forge/NeoForge integration has AntiXray but no Grim behavior engine. Known third-party warnings are retained; fake ore proof is limited to the controlled Overworld fixture.",
    "The optional catalog contains 31 source-backed exact IDs, not a universal cheat database. Existing default 11 rules and administrator choices are preserved."
  ]
